Subject: [PATCH] Build the original CoreCLR3.1 native runtime with Clang20

Preserve original Release optimization, R2R, profiling and LTTng tracing.
Backport the two metadata allocation-marker hunks from upstream commit
35a39e97345abfda05e14f609759760b37ddeb4d, preserving the old NumItems spelling.
Make intentional raw-memory destinations explicit void pointers without changing
addresses, pointer adjustments or byte counts. Preserve actual unsigned enum
storage and signed one-bit register representation, independently byte-checked.
Correct invalid unused template names, keep the existing GNU C++ VLA diagnostic
visible, and suppress only the upstream disabled unused-variable subcategory.
DAC guards exclude three runtime-only reflection-cache mutators; layout and
normal runtime behavior remain unchanged. No vendor binary or feature disable.

Base-CoreCLR: c17d273aa03d4b9d14c92248a91f0d0faa881b98
Apply-After: 0002-clang20-typed-null.patch

--- a/configurecompiler.cmake
+++ b/configurecompiler.cmake
@@ -480,6 +480,8 @@
 
   # Disabled common warnings
   add_compile_options(-Wno-unused-variable)
+  # Modern Clang separates this from the existing unused-variable category.
+  add_compile_options(-Wno-unused-but-set-variable)
   add_compile_options(-Wno-unused-value)
   add_compile_options(-Wno-unused-function)
 
@@ -493,6 +495,9 @@
     # The -ferror-limit is helpful during the porting, it makes sure the compiler doesn't stop
     # after hitting just about 20 errors.
     add_compile_options(-ferror-limit=4096)
+
+    # Existing GNU C++ variable-length arrays remain a visible compatibility warning.
+    add_compile_options($<$<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:CXX>:-Wno-error=vla-cxx-extension>)
 
     # Disabled warnings
     add_compile_options(-Wno-unused-private-field)
